    {
      "file": "",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "Register a Regular Web App in your tenant",
      "description": "## Register a Regular Web App in your tenant\nBefore you can begin configuring the application for authentication, it must be registered in the Auth0 dashboard. Let's do that now.\n\n1. Log in to your Auth0 dashboard at [manage.auth0.com](https://manage.auth0.com). \n\n1. If you have multiple tenants, ensure you have your default **dev-** tenant selected.\n\n1. Go to **Applications** > **Applications**.\n\n1. Select the **+ Create Application** button.\n1. Name the application **Lab: Web App**.\n> Note: It is important that this name be exact, since the Auth0 Labs Extension searches for this name in a subsequent step.\n1. Select **Regular Web Applications**.\n1. Select the **Create** button.\n> You're ready to begin adding authentication to your application\n"
    }
  ]
}